u}$ of a spectral line is given by the Rydberg formula:<br><br>$ ar{
u} = R_H Z^2 \left( \dfrac{1}{n_1^2} - \dfrac{1}{n_2^2} ight)$<br><br>For the $	ext{Li}^{2+}$ ion, the atomic number $Z = 3$.<br><br>For the Paschen series, the lower energy level is $n_1 = 3$. The second line of the Paschen series corresponds to the transition from $n_2 = 5$ to $n_1 = 3$.<br><br>Substituting these values into the formula:<br><br>$ ar{
u} = 109677 	imes 3^2 	imes \left( \dfrac{1}{3^2} - \dfrac{1}{5^2} ight)$<br><br>$ ar{
u} = 109677 	imes 9 	imes \left( \dfrac{1}{9} - \dfrac{1}{25} ight)$<br><br>$ ar{
u} = 109677 	imes 9 	imes \left( \dfrac{25 - 9}{9 	imes 25} ight)$<br><br>$ ar{
u} = 109677 	imes \dfrac{16}{25}$<br><br>$ ar{
u} = 70193.28 	ext{ cm}^{-1}$<br><br>This can be written as $7.019328 	imes 10^4 	ext{ cm}^{-1}$.<br><br>Comparing with $x 	imes 10^4 	ext{ cm}^{-1}$, we get $x = 7.019328$.<br><br>Rounding to the nearest integer, the value of $x$ is $7$.<br><br>Answer: $7$

